{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/118697","id":3547800424,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7TdyNo","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118697","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118697.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118697.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118697","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/118697/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/118697/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118697/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/2295956996b5e074a6ccc3a5ce8bff2d3996bcd7","number":118697,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"fix: RID leak exhausts Godot element pool after 2-5 min (#257)","user":{"login":"klausi3D","id":103386187,"node_id":"U_kgDOBimMSw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/103386187?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/klausi3D","html_url":"https://github.com/klausi3D","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/klausi3D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/klausi3D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/klausi3D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/klausi3D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/klausi3D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/klausi3D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/klausi3D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/klausi3D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/klausi3D/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\n\n- **Root cause:** `RenderDeviceManager::free_owned_resource()` skipped `device->free()` for auto-free-typed resources (uniform sets, compute/render pipelines, framebuffers), assuming Godot's dependency-based auto-free would handle cleanup. Auto-free only triggers when the *referenced* resources (buffers/textures) are freed — since those are long-lived, the uniform sets accumulated forever. The instance pipeline leaked 3 uniform sets per frame (~10,800/min at 60fps), exhausting the RID pool in 2-5 minutes.\n- **Fix:** Check validity and explicitly free auto-free-typed resources before forgetting them. The validity guard (`*_is_valid()`) prevents double-free if the dependency system already cleaned up.\n- **BitonicSort:** `sort()` dropped old uniform sets without freeing, relying on the same broken assumption. Now explicitly frees if still valid.\n- **PainterlyMaterialManager:** `stroke_density_buffer` was overwritten without freeing in `clear_resources()` and `update_resources()` — same bug family.\n- **OneSweepSort:** `wait_for_completion()` cleared the uniform_sets vector without freeing. Now uses `_free_uniform_sets_safe()`.\n- **Test:** Added regression test verifying tracked uniform sets are explicitly freed through `free_owned_resource`.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] Build succeeds (`scons platform=windows target=editor dev_build=yes -j16`)\n- [x] GrandmasHouse editor runs 3+ minutes with zero `Element limit reached` / `\"mem\" is null` / `Failed to create uniform set for batch` errors (previously crashed within 2-5 min)\n- [x] 60-second smoke test: `grep -c \"Element limit\\|mem.*is null\\|Failed to create uniform\"` → 0\n- [ ] Verify painterly material changes don't regress (toggle PainterlyMaterial on/off in editor)\n- [ ] Run unit tests with `tests=yes` build to verify new ownership test passes\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","labels":[{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","descriptio